<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="74663" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/DANC/516/74663.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="DANC" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/DANC.xml">Dance</subject><course id="516" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/DANC/516.xml">Dancing Techniques Graduate Elective</course></parents><sectionNumber>L  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Elect Grad Tech: Int. Ballet</sectionTitle><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course begins with ballet basics; terminology; foundational movements, and ballet etiquette, with an intent to progress over the semester to take a full ballet class with work at a ballet barre and at the center of the room. This class will focus on training the body and muscles in turnout, ballet's relationship to classical music, and discussing ballet history and locality in comparison with current times. Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign. THIS COURSE MEETS FROM 13:00-14:20.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>01:00 PM</start><end>02:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2127</roomNumber><buildingName>Krannert Center for Perf Arts</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Barbier" firstName="A">Barbier, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>